00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:03.907
what's your stance on investing
in competitive companies?

00:09:03.907 --> 00:09:05.366
- Meaning?

00:09:05.366 --> 00:09:07.026
Like for me as a fund.

00:09:07.026 --> 00:09:08.360
- You as a fund, you individually

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.332
- Don't, guys.

00:09:09.332 --> 00:09:10.574
- [Steve] It's gonna
be useless audio though.

00:09:10.574 --> 00:09:12.918
- It's not useless
audio, it's just a horn.

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:16.030
Nobody in the VaynerNation
is concerned about a horn.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.190
- [Steve] They won't
be able to hear the words.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.352
- They'll be able to hear the words.

00:09:18.352 --> 00:09:19.698
Do you think they'll be
able to hear the words?

00:09:19.698 --> 00:09:20.197
- Yeah.

00:09:20.197 --> 00:09:20.893
- Can we hear the words.

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:23.413
I get it and I love you
supporting your teammate DRock.

00:09:23.413 --> 00:09:25.271
I see what you're doing.
I love the support.

00:09:25.271 --> 00:09:30.054
But that horn, this fire truck,

00:09:30.054 --> 00:09:31.771
is adding to the ambiance

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:33.338
of the fact that we're sitting

00:09:33.338 --> 00:09:34.526
in New York City.

00:09:34.526 --> 00:09:36.186
Like we're not sitting in our normal room.

00:09:36.186 --> 00:09:37.266
They'll deal with it.

00:09:37.266 --> 00:09:38.053
Right DRock?

00:09:38.053 --> 00:09:38.854
Alright, thank you.

00:09:38.854 --> 00:09:40.390
It pains you right?

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:41.831
It's like the editor in you just like

00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:44.852
can't deal with, now the horns are coming.

00:09:44.852 --> 00:09:47.348
This is just pouring it on you.

00:09:47.348 --> 00:09:48.507
We're sticking with it.

00:09:48.507 --> 00:09:51.705
So, if I'm a fund, for example,

00:09:51.705 --> 00:09:53.293
when I was an investor in Gowalla

00:09:53.293 --> 00:09:55.790
and there was a chance
to invest in Foursquare.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.402
I didn't, but I know
people that have invested

00:09:58.402 --> 00:09:59.176
in similar companies.

00:09:59.176 --> 00:10:01.507
Are you asking me like
to put my VC hat on?

00:10:01.507 --> 00:10:02.435
- Yeah.
- And angel hat.

00:10:02.435 --> 00:10:04.273
You know, look I think,
there's two answers.

00:10:04.273 --> 00:10:06.216
One I think, if you're
investing in a company

00:10:06.216 --> 00:10:07.975
and then there's a chance
to invest in somebody

00:10:07.975 --> 00:10:09.489
who's a direct competitor

00:10:09.489 --> 00:10:12.080
and that company wants you to do that.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:13.033
That seems to me like ...

00:10:13.043 --> 00:10:14.193
(sirens blaring)

00:10:14.193 --> 00:10:15.127
(laughing)

00:10:15.127 --> 00:10:17.577
That seems to me like a
little bit of a dick move.

00:10:17.577 --> 00:10:20.852
What I'm more worried about
is the problem I'm facing now.

00:10:20.852 --> 00:10:23.173
(sirens blaring)

00:10:23.173 --> 00:10:23.927
I'll be quiet for you.

00:10:23.927 --> 00:10:25.030
This is me doing a nice thing for you.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:27.235
But the tape is running,
the tape is running.

00:10:27.235 --> 00:10:29.112
- It better be.

00:10:29.112 --> 00:10:32.822
- To me the bigger problem is the pivot.

00:10:32.822 --> 00:10:34.202
Right now my biggest problem is

00:10:34.202 --> 00:10:36.303
I'm investing in companies that
are a little bit different.

00:10:36.303 --> 00:10:37.720
But I can see an entrepreneur

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.623
how one move by each product

00:10:39.623 --> 00:10:41.819
gets them in to a competitive space.

00:10:41.819 --> 00:10:44.441
My answer is, you go in with the open eyes

00:10:44.441 --> 00:10:45.997
and honesty that you can.

00:10:45.997 --> 00:10:48.341
But you can't fight against
the fact that people

00:10:48.341 --> 00:10:49.340
are competing with each other.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.639
As we now live in a world
where the cost of entry

00:10:51.639 --> 00:10:53.416
to compete with each
other is so much lower.

00:10:53.416 --> 00:10:55.133
I think you should go in
with the right intentions.

00:10:55.133 --> 00:10:56.817
Your reputate, by the way,

00:10:56.817 --> 00:11:00.173
the only reason I think you
should be a good guy or gal

00:11:00.173 --> 00:11:01.634
and not invest in a competitor,

00:11:01.634 --> 00:11:05.060
is because your reputation is your equity.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.162
Like it's selfish.

00:11:06.162 --> 00:11:07.858
It's cause I want to be
able to invest in things

00:11:07.858 --> 00:11:08.716
in the future.

00:11:08.716 --> 00:11:10.457
And if I have a reputation
for constantly investing

00:11:10.457 --> 00:11:13.035
in my competitive stuff just
to win on short term money,

00:11:13.035 --> 00:11:14.741
I'm not gonna be able to get into deals.

00:11:14.741 --> 00:11:16.474
So I think reputation management

00:11:16.474 --> 00:11:18.273
in a transparent world matters.

00:11:18.273 --> 00:11:21.594
I think that is a dick
move, if you're doing that.

00:11:21.594 --> 00:11:22.197
- Gotcha.

00:11:22.197 --> 00:11:23.495
- Is that basically
answering your question?

00:11:23.495 --> 00:11:25.470
